# ---- POINTER: HELD AT dbus-rel, PENDING THE CUTOVER ITSELF ----
# The absolute pointer for this station is BUILT AND PROVEN AT THE DEVICE
# LEVEL and is not yet cut over. It is NOT blocked on a sink defect; an
# earlier version of this header said it was, and that was wrong.
#
# WHAT ACTUALLY HAPPENED ON rhapsody (settled 2026-08-31 by a four-run control
# matrix, {ramabs, dbus-rel} x {observer running, observer absent}):
# the failure was DAEMON-WIDE QMP CONTENTION CAUSED BY THE OBSERVATION
# HARNESS, and had nothing to do with the pointer backend.
#   * The acceptance run's observer (`observe.py`) held QEMU's QMP monitor for
#     its whole run. QEMU serves ONE monitor at a time.
#   * So the idle pauser's `cont` hit its 2 s socket timeout (idle.rs) and
#     returned EAGAIN.
#   * `IdlePauser::session_started()` holds the `st` mutex ACROSS that blocking
#     call, and `handle_session` awaits it BEFORE any priming/keyframe work --
#     deliberately, to resume a paused guest first.
#   * Every session therefore serialised behind that stall and blew the SPA's
#     negotiation timeout. Hence 40 SESSION_ACCEPTED with zero completed.
#   * `dbus-rel` -- which builds NO InputRouter at all, `from_config` returns
#     None for it -- fails IDENTICALLY while the holder is running.
# The original isolation compared `ramabs` WITH the observer against `dbus-rel`
# WITHOUT it, so the one variable that mattered was never controlled.
#
# The code corroborates this independently of the matrix: `RealtimeInputSink`
# has NO session lifecycle hook at all, and `InputRouter` is built ONCE per
# station in `transport::serve`, outside the accept loop -- so there is no
# per-session sink state that could leak, which makes the old diagnosis
# impossible rather than merely unlikely. And `ram_abs.rs` is byte-identical to
# `mga_ctl.rs` apart from names, which runs live on aix432 (46 SESSION_ACCEPTED
# / 46 SESSION_ENDED over three days). `artist_ctl.rs` is identical too, apart
# from the paused-guest ack grace below.
#
# THE STANDING LESSON IS ABOUT THE OBSERVER, NOT THE SINK: an acceptance
# harness that holds the QMP monitor changes the behaviour it is measuring, and
# a comparison that moves the harness and the backend together cannot attribute
# what it sees. Control the observer; vary one thing at a time.
#
# THE DAEMON NOW ACCEPTS artistctl (checked 2026-08-31). An earlier reading had
# this station on streamhost-bcaaecb, whose accepted-value list ended at
# `mgactl`, making the env flip impossible before a canary install. That is no
# longer the state: the running daemon is
# streamhost-b582141de890f18a7d66f27db0905a5ca0376872 (since 08:43), and asked
# for its own list -- by feeding it an invalid backend rather than by grepping
# the binary -- it answers `...|mgactl|artistctl|ramabs`. So the artifact half
# of the ordering is satisfied and only the flip itself remains.
#
# TO COMPLETE THIS CUTOVER, together: set
# SH_INPUT_BACKEND=artistctl here AND flip the registry's
# stream.pointer / spa.pointerRel / operator.labctl.pointer_mode / reset.pointer /
# runtime.qemu.emitArgs, operator.labctl.notes, operator.actionMap.value.note
# and runtime.qemu.deviceSetSummary (these last three are the easy ones to
# miss: the two note fields are what an operator READS and would describe a
# relative pointer on a station that is no longer relative -- labctl.notes is
# also compared by the live-labctl gate check -- and deviceSetSummary must
# name the -chardev/-global artist.ptrctl pair the launcher actually starts).
# The QEMU binary and launcher are already installed and need no change.
#
# ---- INSTALLED BINARY / LAUNCHER PAIRING - DO NOT SPLIT ----
# READ THIS FIRST IF QEMU REFUSES TO START ON THIS STATION.
# /opt/qemu-hppa/bin/qemu-system-hppa
# was REPLACED on 2026-08-30 with a build carrying the absolute-pointer
# patches, and the previous binary was kept beside it as
# <same path>.pre-abs-bak. The deployed launcher was updated in the same
# pass and now passes `-global artist.ptrctl=`, which the .pre-abs-bak binary
# DOES NOT SUPPORT (verified against the binaries, not the patch series).
# NOT YET RESTARTED onto this pair -- its running QEMU still holds the OLD
# inode. The next restart, for ANY reason, is the first exercise of it.
#
# THE PAIR IS BINDING IN BOTH DIRECTIONS. Restoring .pre-abs-bak while the
# current launcher stays installed makes QEMU refuse to start outright --
# artist.ptrctl is an unknown property on that build. Rolling this station back to the
# old binary means restoring the OLD LAUNCHER TOO, in the same pass.
# Both new or both old. Never mixed.
#
# The pointer BACKEND is a separate axis and is safe to move alone: the
# device is armed in the launcher but nothing connects to ptr.sock while
# SH_INPUT_BACKEND=dbus-rel, which is the state this station is in.

# ---- CHECKPOINT FIXTURE (QEMU station, resetMode=loadvm) ----
# The scene is the HP VUE 3.0 desktop as root on HP-UX 10.20, 1280x1024x8
# over the Artist framebuffer: front panel with six workspaces, the Helpview
# "Welcome to Your HP Workstation!" window and one File Manager on "/".
# Baked 2026-08-18 with savevm into the station-local hpuxvue-golden.qcow2
# (the CD stays attached with the same ISO so the device set is loadvm-exact).
SH_RESET_MODE=loadvm
SH_GOLDEN_SNAPSHOT=golden
SH_FIXTURE_DESC=HP VUE 3.0 desktop (HP-UX 10.20, HP 9000/778 B160L under TCG) at 1280x1024x8: front panel, Helpview welcome, one File Manager. loadvm restores the desktop; the guest starts frozen (-S) until the first visitor.

# ---- POINTER: RELATIVE LASI PS/2, and why the scale IS 1.0 ----
# The B160L has no absolute pointer path (no USB, no tablet), so the daemon
# runs its abs->rel bridge. Measured 2026-08-18: 50 units -> 96 px on both
# axes, which is exactly X's default acceleration (2x beyond a 4-px
# threshold), not a hardware factor. /.vue/sessionetc runs `xset m 1 1` at
# session start (VUE re-applies its own mouse settings over the server
# default, like CDE), after which 50 units -> 50 px. So SH_CURSOR_SCALE is a
# true 1.0. If the checkpoint is ever re-baked without sessionetc, the pointer
# will overshoot ~2x.
SH_INPUT_BACKEND=dbus-rel
SH_CURSOR_SCALE=1.0

# ---- IDLE AUTO-PAUSE: ON ----
# hppa runs under TCG only, so an idle station burns a host core for nobody.
# Plain QEMU station: the daemon's default QMP stop/cont path applies. The
# launcher starts the guest PAUSED at the checkpoint (-loadvm golden -S), so
# an unvisited station never runs a guest instruction. Warmup 0: there is no
# boot to protect. Rollback: SH_IDLE_PAUSE_SECS=0.
SH_IDLE_PAUSE_SECS=60
